From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rory Axton <roryaxton@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:13:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 0932 redfin: /dev/redwood-camera mode classes, warm mode
 switch, table files kept, fallback

SENSOR's c picks the mode when b is ~0: 0 auto / 1 photo (the most pixels at
4:3, <= 31 fps, <= 13 MP), 2 video (16:9, <= 4096 wide, >= 1600x900, >= 29.5
fps: the lowest frame rate, then the fewest pixels), 3 video60 (the same from
59 fps; video where there is none). From the module files: IMX363 photo 0
4032x3024, video 10 2016x1136@30, video60 9 2016x1136@60; IMX355 photo 0
3280x2464, video 2 1640x924@30 (no 60); IMX481 photo 7 2328x1746, video and
video60 3 2328x1310@60.

The same sensor and mode asked for again changes nothing; another mode of the
streaming sensor is switched without a power cycle (frames stopped at a
frame's end, receive path down; the new mode's table, the exposure clamped to
it, the places re-made if larger -- not while a read copies -- the receive
path and "on" again); the first frame after a sensor or mode change carries
MODE_CHANGED (reserved[0] bit 2). A sensor that cannot be selected leaves the
previous one selected instead of giving the device up. The table files are
read once and kept ("c 23" forgets them).
